# L §5.10: a keyed `place` section gives each instance the section's unit, so bal(wc[k], d) is `num PLN` (money PLN)
# like an unkeyed place's; units[a] = round(100 PLN / 10 PLN/u1, 1 u1, down) = 10 u1 (L §7.2).  Was LOAD-UNIT (dyn).
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-10
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-01-31
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
unit u1 "jednostka"
index w = [a, b]
index month = month 2026-01..2026-01
place wc[k in w]: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
input px: num PLN/u1
def units[k in w, m in month]: num u1 = round(bal(wc[k], start_of(m)) / px, 1 u1, down) at start_of(m)
source s "x"
version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  px = 10
  opening[wc[a]] = 100 at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[wc[b]] = 0 at 2026-01-01 start
ask q: units[a, 2026-01] law cut
=== expect
q: 10 u1
  law date 2026-01-10, cut 2026-01-10
